ION_AUTHORITY_INDEX.md"}]},"recipient":"all","channel":"commentary"},{"id":"e19a94cd-ab41-4b06-a65b-171e4f21bdb4","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1790231164.580199,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"thoughts","thoughts":[{"summary":"Planning the requested ArcheAxis audit","content":"I’m identifying the scope and required outputs for a Chinese deep-research audit of the ArcheAxis project, including repositories, branches, documentation, workflows, integrations, governance, traceability, and unresolved work.\n\nThe request emphasizes evidence-backed findings, comparisons with prior conclusions, P0–P2 remediation, YAML and Mermaid examples, inaccessible-item disclosure, and reproducible follow-up prompts.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Assessing repository governance and audit evidence","content":"I’m consolidating the newly identified repository evidence. The project has multiple unprotected branches, one merged pull request, and recent CI failures requiring inspection. Its governance documents define authority order, audit receipts, append-only records, and safeguards against silent dependency or cloud-tool changes.\n\nI’m also noting that the connected workspace search found no matching project records, which doesn’t prove they’re absent elsewhere.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Planned the ArcheAxis audit and assessed repository governance evidence","content":"","chunks":[],"finished":true}],"source_analysis_msg_id":"dca078da-c294-4b91-9864-8e57d49f677a"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"reasoning_status":"is_reasoning"},"recipient":"all","channel":null},{"id":"b70d58cb-1d17-4302-ba90-634b4f681be0","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1790231464.357833,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"reasoning_recap","content":"Worked for 8m 43s"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"r